{
  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) achieves 0.527 acc, only ~4.2% above RNA-only (config_001, 0.485), while image-only (config_010) is very weak at 0.208. This suggests the image modality contributes modestly under the current singleprofile setup. Uncertainty: the multiprofile axis is completely untested across all three modalities, and it is a major structural design choice that could substantially change how image (and RNA) information is aggregated before fusion. Question: config_018 keeps the exact same encoders (pca_n2000, resnet50) and fusion (concat) as config_016 but switches to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation, isolating the effect of multi-view aggregation. Why best next step: it is a controlled, single-axis extension of the current best configuration, so any performance shift is attributable to the profile/aggregation change. A positive result would validate multiprofile as a productive direction and unlock a large family of follow-up experiments (better encoders, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion); a null or negative result would efficiently rule out multiprofile and refocus the budget on encoder or fusion improvements. Under a limited budget, resolving this high-uncertainty structural axis before investing in more expensive encoder swaps maximizes information per experiment."
}

